# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the making of this lesson, from the extrapolation to the zero-noise case, we get an expectation value of 0.959. Your values might differ. This is substantially better than the raw circuit's expectation value of 0.83, around 13% closer to the ideal value. But you can also see that we are using one data point where the expectation value was down at 0.31. Obviously this data point is of poorer quality. If that data point had been given lower weighting in our linear approximation, and the line were fitted more to the first two data points, we can see the zero-extrapolated estimate would have been higher (nearer the ideal value). This sort of consideration is handled automatically in the ZNE built into Estimator.\n"
msgstr "Sa paggawa ng lesson na ito, mula sa extrapolation papunta sa zero-noise na kaso, nakakuha tayo ng expectation value na 0.959. Maaaring iba ang mga halaga mo. Mas mahusay ito nang malaki kaysa sa expectation value ng raw circuit na 0.83, mga 13% na mas malapit sa ideal na halaga. Pero makikita mo rin na gumagamit tayo ng isang data point kung saan ang expectation value ay bumaba sa 0.31. Malinaw na mas mababa ang kalidad ng data point na ito. Kung mas mababa ang timbang na ibinigay sa data point na iyon sa linear approximation natin, at ang linya ay mas na-fit sa unang dalawang data point, makikita nating mas mataas sana (mas malapit sa ideal na halaga) ang zero-extrapolated na tantiya. Awtomatikong hinahawakan ang ganitong konsiderasyon sa ZNE na built-in sa Estimator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE built into Estimator {#zne-built-into-estimator}"
msgstr "ZNE na built-in sa Estimator {#zne-built-into-estimator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let's see what happens when we use the ZNE functionality built into Estimator. We start by defining a simple GHZ circuit, without any gate folding.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon tingnan natin kung ano ang mangyayari kapag ginamit natin ang ZNE functionality na built-in sa Estimator. Magsisimula tayo sa pagtukoy ng simpleng GHZ circuit, na walang gate folding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We define the same observable as before.\n"
msgstr "Tinutukoy natin ang parehong observable gaya ng dati.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We once again define a pass manager, using `optimization_level = 1`. We will return to this choice below.\n"
msgstr "Muli tayong magtatakda ng pass manager, gamit ang `optimization_level = 1`. Babalikan natin ang pagpiling ito sa ibaba.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile the circuit and apply the layout to the observables.\n"
msgstr "I-transpile ang circuit at ilapat ang layout sa mga observable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We run the Estimator using ZNE and twirling, and we compare the outcomes to our ZNE by-hand implementation. In particular, we compare them to the result without ZNE (`value_no_zne`).\n"
msgstr "Pinatatakbo natin ang Estimator gamit ang ZNE at twirling, at ikinukumpara ang mga kinalabasan sa by-hand na implementasyon natin ng ZNE. Partikular, ikinukumpara natin ang mga ito sa resultang walang ZNE (`value_no_zne`).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can retrieve the values at each noise factor using the syntax `job_zne.result()[0].data.evs_noise_factors`. As before, we could naively use these results to get a linear fit and extrapolate to the zero-noise case, but the estimator with `resilience_level = 2` has already done a better job, taking variance and other considerations into account. Below we show what a linear extrapolation would yield, and we show what built-in ZNE actually yielded.\n"
msgstr "Makukuha natin ang mga halaga sa bawat noise factor gamit ang syntax na `job_zne.result()[0].data.evs_noise_factors`. Gaya ng dati, maaari nating gamitin nang naive ang mga resultang ito para makakuha ng linear fit at mag-extrapolate sa zero-noise na kaso, pero mas maayos na ang nagawa ng estimator na may `resilience_level = 2`, dahil isinasaalang-alang nito ang variance at iba pang konsiderasyon. Sa ibaba ipinapakita natin kung ano ang ibibigay ng linear extrapolation, at kung ano ang aktwal na ibinigay ng built-in na ZNE.\n"

