msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/d54a12ec-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We see that the built-in ZNE improved our estimate by over 15%, and worked quite a bit better than our attempt by hand.\n"
msgstr "Nakikita nating pinabuti ng built-in na ZNE ang tantiya natin nang mahigit 15%, at mas mahusay nang malaki kaysa sa pagsubok nating gawin ito nang mano-mano.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before moving on, note that throughout this ZNE exploration, we have set `optimization_level = 1` in the pass manager. Higher levels of optimization reduce error, and sometimes the error reduction can make the errors scale less predictably. As is often the case, there is a balance: reduce errors, except when you are intentionally increasing them by a known factor.\n"
msgstr "Bago magpatuloy, tandaan na sa buong ZNE exploration na ito, itinakda natin ang `optimization_level = 1` sa pass manager. Binabawasan ng mas matataas na level ng optimization ang error, at minsan ang pagbawas ng error ay nagpapahirap hulaan ang pag-scale ng mga error. Gaya ng madalas mangyari, may balanse: bawasan ang mga error, maliban kung sinasadya mo silang taasan nang may kilalang factor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Combining methods {#combining-methods}"
msgstr "Pagsasama ng mga method {#combining-methods}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE relies on the following:\n"
msgstr "Umaasa ang ZNE sa mga sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A well-defined noise-scaling parameter $\\lambda$\n"
msgstr "Isang malinaw na tinukoy na noise-scaling parameter na $\\lambda$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sufficiently smooth and predictable scaling of expectation values with $\\lambda$\n"
msgstr "Sapat na maayos at predictable na pag-scale ng mga expectation value kasabay ng $\\lambda$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same effective noise channel, at different strengths\n"
msgstr "Parehong epektibong noise channel, sa magkakaibang lakas\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "No bias introduced that does not scale with $\\lambda$\n"
msgstr "Walang ipinasok na bias na hindi nag-i-scale kasabay ng $\\lambda$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE combines cleanly with techniques that remove non-scaling biases (like M3) or make noise more regular (like twirling), but conflicts with techniques that either attempt to cancel noise entirely (PEC) or reshape it dynamically (DD).\n"
msgstr "Maayos na naisasama ang ZNE sa mga technique na nag-aalis ng mga bias na hindi nag-i-scale (tulad ng M3) o ginagawang mas regular ang noise (tulad ng twirling), pero sumasalungat ito sa mga technique na sinusubukang kanselahin nang buo ang noise (PEC) o hubugin ito nang dynamic (DD).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In particular, M3 addresses only measurement/readout error, which in practice can be treated as separate from gate errors (which are the focus of error scaling processes in ZNE). M3 is largely independent of gate folding; it can be cleanly combined with ZNE. TREX is very similar, and it can be combined with ZNE.\n"
msgstr "Sa partikular, ang M3 ay tumutugon lang sa measurement/readout error, na sa praktika ay maaaring ituring na hiwalay sa mga gate error (na siyang pokus ng mga proseso ng error scaling sa ZNE). Halos independent ang M3 sa gate folding; maaari itong maayos na isama sa ZNE. Halos magkapareho ang TREX, at maaari rin itong isama sa ZNE.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling does focus on gates, unlike M3 and TREX. However, recall that Pauli twirling does not directly mitigate error/noise; rather, it changes it to make it more predictable. Pauli twirling might actually be beneficial to the ZNE process in making gate errors scale more linearly and thus make the extrapolation more accurate.\n"
msgstr "Nakatuon ang Pauli twirling sa mga gate, hindi tulad ng M3 at TREX. Gayunpaman, tandaan na hindi direktang binabawasan ng Pauli twirling ang error/noise; sa halip, binabago nito ito para maging mas predictable. Maaaring makatulong ang Pauli twirling sa proseso ng ZNE dahil mas nagiging linear ang pag-scale ng mga gate error kaya mas tumpak ang extrapolation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dynamical decoupling (DD) is more nuanced. DD dynamically alters noise behavior by partially cancelling certain errors through the addition of gate sequences. If it is possible to construct circuits in such a way that DD behaves the same even when gates or blocks are folded, then in principle one could combine ZNE and DD, but in practice DD sometimes interferes with the scaling. If you want to combine them, things to consider include the following:\n"
"* Is DD applied consistently at all noise levels?\n"
"* Does folding preserve the DD structure?\n"
"* Does the resulting noise scaling still behave monotonically?\n"
msgstr ""
"Mas may nuance ang Dynamical decoupling (DD). Dynamic na binabago ng DD ang pagkilos ng noise sa pamamagitan ng bahagyang pagkansela ng ilang error sa pagdaragdag ng mga gate sequence. Kung posibleng buuin ang mga circuit sa paraang pareho ang kilos ng DD kahit na naka-fold ang mga gate o block, sa prinsipyo ay maaaring pagsamahin ang ZNE at DD, pero sa praktika minsan nakakasagabal ang DD sa scaling. Kung gusto mong pagsamahin ang mga ito, kabilang sa mga dapat isaalang-alang ang sumusunod:\n"
"* Pare-pareho bang inilalapat ang DD sa lahat ng noise levels?\n"
"* Napapanatili ba ng folding ang istruktura ng DD?\n"
"* Monotonic pa rin ba ang kilos ng resultang noise scaling?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last error mitigation method we will discuss as a standalone approach is not compatible with ZNE: probabilistic error cancellation.\n"
msgstr "Ang huling error mitigation method na tatalakayin natin bilang standalone na approach ay hindi compatible sa ZNE: probabilistic error cancellation.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) {#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec}"
msgstr "Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) {#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unlike ZNE or measurement mitigation, PEC attempts to cancel noise at the gate level by reconstructing the ideal channel in expectation. Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) is the most powerful and most expensive error-mitigation technique covered in this lesson. PEC is built around explicit inversion of the noise channel, carried out statistically rather than physically. PEC works by:\n"
msgstr "Hindi tulad ng ZNE o measurement mitigation, sinusubukan ng PEC na kanselahin ang noise sa antas ng gate sa pamamagitan ng muling pagbuo ng ideal na channel sa expectation. Ang Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) ang pinakamakapangyarihan at pinakamahal na error-mitigation technique na saklaw ng lesson na ito. Binuo ang PEC sa paligid ng tahasang inversion ng noise channel, na isinasagawa nang istatistikal sa halip na pisikal. Ganito gumagana ang PEC:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characterizing the noise model in terms of a basis of \"error operations.\"\n"
msgstr "Pagtukoy sa noise model batay sa isang basis ng \"error operations.\"\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expressing the inverse of the noise channel as a quasi-probability distribution over physical operations.\n"
msgstr "Pagpapahayag ng inverse ng noise channel bilang quasi-probability distribution sa mga pisikal na operasyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampling from this distribution during circuit execution to statistically construct an unbiased estimate of the ideal computation.\n"
msgstr "Pag-sample mula sa distribution na ito habang isinasagawa ang circuit para istatistikal na buuin ang unbiased na tantiya ng ideal na computation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conceptually, PEC is like virtual error correction &mdash; it \"undoes\" noise by combining noisy operations in carefully weighted random patterns. Procedurally, however, PEC is not closely related to error correction or detection code. PEC's unbiased estimation of the ideal, noiseless expectation value comes at the cost of a very large sampling overhead and a strong dependence on accurate noise characterization.\n"
msgstr "Sa konsepto, ang PEC ay parang virtual error correction &mdash; \"binabawi\" nito ang noise sa pamamagitan ng pagsasama ng mga noisy na operasyon sa maingat na tinimbang na random na mga pattern. Sa pamamaraan naman, hindi malapit na kaugnay ng error correction o detection code ang PEC. Ang unbiased na pagtantiya ng PEC sa ideal at noiseless na expectation value ay may kapalit na napakalaking sampling overhead at malakas na pagdepende sa tumpak na noise characterization.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On IBM quantum computers, PEC is best viewed as a precision tool rather than a general-purpose mitigation layer: it is most appropriate for small circuits or small portions of larger circuits, benchmarking tasks, and high-accuracy studies where high quantum overhead is acceptable.\n"
msgstr "Sa mga IBM quantum computer, pinakamainam tingnan ang PEC bilang precision tool kaysa general-purpose na mitigation layer: pinakaangkop ito sa maliliit na circuit o maliliit na bahagi ng mas malalaking circuit, mga benchmarking task, at mga high-accuracy na pag-aaral kung saan katanggap-tanggap ang mataas na quantum overhead.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characterizing the noise channel {#characterizing-the-noise-channel}"
msgstr "Pagtukoy sa noise channel {#characterizing-the-noise-channel}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In PEC, each ideal gate in a quantum circuit is modeled as an **ideal unitary channel** followed by a noise process. Let $\\rho$ denote the density matrix of the quantum state. The ideal gate is represented by a unitary matrix $U$, which induces a quantum channel:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{U}(\\rho) = U\\,\\rho\\,U^\\dagger.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa PEC, ang bawat ideal na gate sa isang quantum circuit ay minomodelo bilang isang **ideal unitary channel** na sinusundan ng noise process. Ipagpalagay na ang $\\rho$ ang density matrix ng quantum state. Ang ideal na gate ay kinakatawan ng unitary matrix na $U$, na lumilikha ng quantum channel:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{U}(\\rho) = U\\,\\rho\\,U^\\dagger.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On real hardware, this ideal evolution is corrupted by noise. We model the physical implementation of the gate as an **effective noisy channel**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(\\mathcal{U}(\\rho)\\right)\n"
"= \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(U\\rho U^\\dagger\\right),\n"
"$$\n"
"where $\\mathcal{N}$ is a noise channel capturing the stochastic errors associated with the gate. Throughout this discussion, $\\mathcal{U}$, $\\mathcal{N}$, and $\\mathcal{E}$ are linear maps acting on density operators. The ideal channel $\\mathcal{U}$ is unitary and reversible, while the noise channel $\\mathcal{N}$ (and hence $\\mathcal{E}$) is a completely positive, trace-preserving (CPTP) map.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa totoong hardware, sinisira ng noise ang ideal na ebolusyong ito. Minomodelo natin ang pisikal na implementasyon ng gate bilang isang **effective noisy channel**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(\\mathcal{U}(\\rho)\\right)\n"
"= \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(U\\rho U^\\dagger\\right),\n"
"$$\n"
"kung saan ang $\\mathcal{N}$ ay noise channel na kumakatawan sa mga stochastic error na kaugnay ng gate. Sa buong talakayang ito, ang $\\mathcal{U}$, $\\mathcal{N}$, at $\\mathcal{E}$ ay mga linear map na kumikilos sa density operators. Ang ideal na channel na $\\mathcal{U}$ ay unitary at reversible, habang ang noise channel na $\\mathcal{N}$ (at kaya ang $\\mathcal{E}$) ay isang completely positive, trace-preserving (CPTP) map.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC assumes that the noise channel $\\mathcal{N}$ is known or approximately known. On IBM Quantum hardware, this information is typically obtained from device calibration data, error rates inferred from benchmarking experiments, and simplified noise models such as Pauli or depolarizing approximations for small gate sets. While PEC does not require a perfectly accurate noise model, its performance degrades rapidly as the assumed noise channel diverges from the true hardware behavior.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapalagay ng PEC na kilala o halos kilala ang noise channel na $\\mathcal{N}$. Sa IBM Quantum hardware, karaniwang nakukuha ang impormasyong ito mula sa device calibration data, mga error rate na hinuha mula sa benchmarking experiments, at mga pinasimpleng noise model tulad ng Pauli o depolarizing approximations para sa maliliit na gate set. Bagaman hindi kailangan ng PEC ng ganap na tumpak na noise model, mabilis na bumababa ang performance nito habang lumalayo ang ipinapalagay na noise channel sa tunay na kilos ng hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quasi-probability decomposition of the inverse noise channel {#quasi-probability-decomposition-of-the-inverse-noise-channel}"
msgstr "Quasi-probability decomposition ng inverse noise channel {#quasi-probability-decomposition-of-the-inverse-noise-channel}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The central idea of PEC is to **cancel the effect of noise in expectation** by constructing a stochastic approximation to the inverse of the noise channel. Formally, the goal is to apply a linear map that approximately undoes $\\mathcal{N}$, such that:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} \\circ \\mathcal{E} \\;\\approx\\; \\mathcal{U}\n"
"$$\n"
"in expectation over many circuit executions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pangunahing ideya ng PEC ay **kanselahin ang epekto ng noise sa expectation** sa pamamagitan ng pagbuo ng stochastic approximation sa inverse ng noise channel. Pormal, ang layunin ay maglapat ng linear map na humigit-kumulang bumabawi sa $\\mathcal{N}$, upang:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} \\circ \\mathcal{E} \\;\\approx\\; \\mathcal{U}\n"
"$$\n"
"sa expectation sa maraming circuit execution.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The inverse $\\mathcal{N}^{-1}$ is defined here as the algebraic inverse of $\\mathcal{N}$ treated as a linear superoperator acting on operators. This inverse exists only if $\\mathcal{N}$ is full-rank; non-invertible noise processes cannot be exactly mitigated using PEC.\n"
msgstr "Ang inverse na $\\mathcal{N}^{-1}$ ay tinutukoy dito bilang algebraic inverse ng $\\mathcal{N}$ na itinuturing na linear superoperator na kumikilos sa mga operator. Umiiral lang ang inverse na ito kung full-rank ang $\\mathcal{N}$; ang mga noise process na hindi invertible ay hindi eksaktong ma-mitigate gamit ang PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When inversion is possible, PEC expresses the inverse noise channel as a **linear combination of physically implementable operations**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} = \\sum_i \\eta_i\\, \\mathcal{O}_i.\n"
"$$\n"
"Here, each $\\mathcal{O}_i$ is a noisy operation that can be executed on the hardware (typically native gates or short gate sequences), and the real coefficients $\\eta_i$ form a **quasi-probability distribution**. Unlike ordinary probabilities, the coefficients $\\eta_i$ might be negative or exceed 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag posible ang inversion, ipinapahayag ng PEC ang inverse noise channel bilang **linear combination ng mga pisikal na maipapatupad na operasyon**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} = \\sum_i \\eta_i\\, \\mathcal{O}_i.\n"
"$$\n"
"Dito, ang bawat $\\mathcal{O}_i$ ay noisy na operasyon na maisasagawa sa hardware (karaniwang native gates o maiikling gate sequence), at ang mga tunay na coefficient na $\\eta_i$ ay bumubuo ng **quasi-probability distribution**. Hindi tulad ng ordinaryong probabilities, ang mga coefficient na $\\eta_i$ ay maaaring negatibo o lumampas sa 1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **quasi-probability norm**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma \\equiv \\sum_i |\\eta_i|\n"
"$$\n"
"quantifies the cost of the noise inversion. For any nontrivial noise channel, $\\gamma > 1$. On IBM Quantum hardware, this decomposition is typically performed:\n"
"- per gate or per small gate set,\n"
"- assuming restricted noise models (often Pauli-diagonal approximations),\n"
"- using backend-specific native operations and scheduling constraints.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang **quasi-probability norm**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma \\equiv \\sum_i |\\eta_i|\n"
"$$\n"
"ay sumusukat sa gastos ng noise inversion. Para sa anumang nontrivial na noise channel, $\\gamma > 1$. Sa IBM Quantum hardware, karaniwang ginagawa ang decomposition na ito:\n"
"- kada gate o kada maliit na gate set,\n"
"- sa pag-aakalang restricted ang mga noise model (madalas Pauli-diagonal approximations),\n"
"- gamit ang mga backend-specific na native operation at scheduling constraint.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Monte Carlo reconstruction of the ideal circuit {#monte-carlo-reconstruction-of-the-ideal-circuit}"
msgstr "Monte Carlo reconstruction ng ideal na circuit {#monte-carlo-reconstruction-of-the-ideal-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To estimate the expectation value of an observable $O$, PEC uses Monte Carlo sampling based on the decomposition above. For each occurrence of a noisy gate in the circuit, the following procedure is applied:\n"
msgstr "Para tantiyahin ang expectation value ng observable na $O$, gumagamit ang PEC ng Monte Carlo sampling batay sa decomposition sa itaas. Para sa bawat paglitaw ng noisy na gate sa circuit, inilalapat ang sumusunod na pamamaraan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Randomly select an operation $\\mathcal{O}_i$ with probability:\n"
"$$\n"
"p_i = \\frac{|\\eta_i|}{\\gamma}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Random na pumili ng operasyong $\\mathcal{O}_i$ na may probability:\n"
"$$\n"
"p_i = \\frac{|\\eta_i|}{\\gamma}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assign a classical weight:\n"
"$$\n"
"w_i = \\mathrm{sign}(\\eta_i).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Magtalaga ng classical weight:\n"
"$$\n"
"w_i = \\mathrm{sign}(\\eta_i).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execute the resulting randomized noisy circuit on the quantum backend.\n"
msgstr "I-execute ang resultang randomized noisy circuit sa quantum backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiply the measured outcome by the product of all accumulated weights.\n"
msgstr "I-multiply ang nasukat na outcome sa product ng lahat ng naipong weight.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Average the weighted results over many circuit executions.\n"
msgstr "I-average ang mga weighted na resulta sa maraming circuit execution.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The resulting estimator $\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}$ satisfies\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{E}\\!\\left[\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right] = \\langle O \\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}},\n"
"$$\n"
"provided the noise model $\\mathcal{N}$ accurately describes the hardware. PEC therefore introduces **no systematic bias** in expectation, but replaces bias with **large statistical variance**. Each run produces a noisy but weighted estimate; only after averaging many such runs does the ideal expectation value emerge.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang resultang estimator na $\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}$ ay tumutupad sa\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{E}\\!\\left[\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right] = \\langle O \\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}},\n"
"$$\n"
"basta tumpak na inilalarawan ng noise model na $\\mathcal{N}$ ang hardware. Kaya ang PEC ay nagpapasok ng **walang systematic bias** sa expectation, ngunit pinapalitan ang bias ng **malaking statistical variance**. Bawat run ay gumagawa ng noisy pero weighted na tantiya; pagkatapos lang i-average ang maraming ganoong run lumilitaw ang ideal na expectation value.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conceptual interpretation {#conceptual-interpretation}"
msgstr "Konseptwal na interpretasyon {#conceptual-interpretation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is sometimes described as *virtual error correction*. While this phrasing is not entirely incorrect, it should not be confused with true quantum error correction. PEC involves no logical encoding, no syndrome extraction, and no real-time feedback. Errors are not prevented or corrected during circuit execution.\n"
msgstr "Minsan inilalarawan ang PEC bilang *virtual error correction*. Bagaman hindi lubos na mali ang pananalitang ito, hindi ito dapat ipagkamali sa tunay na quantum error correction. Walang logical encoding, walang syndrome extraction, at walang real-time feedback sa PEC. Hindi napipigilan o naitatama ang mga error habang isinasagawa ang circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead, PEC cancels noise **statistically**, by combining many noisy circuit realizations with signed classical weights so that errors cancel only after classical post-processing. Information is not protected during execution; ideal results are reconstructed after the fact.\n"
msgstr "Sa halip, kinakansela ng PEC ang noise nang **istatistikal**, sa pamamagitan ng pagsasama ng maraming noisy na circuit realization na may signed na classical weights upang magkansela ang mga error pagkatapos lang ng classical post-processing. Hindi pinoprotektahan ang impormasyon habang isinasagawa; muling binubuo ang mga ideal na resulta pagkatapos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Resource scaling and cost {#resource-scaling-and-cost}"
msgstr "Resource scaling at gastos {#resource-scaling-and-cost}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The dominant cost of PEC stems from variance amplification. The variance of the PEC estimator scales as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Var}\\!\\left(\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right) \\propto \\gamma^2,\n"
"$$\n"
"implying:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\boxed{\\text{Required number of shots} \\;\\propto\\; \\gamma^2.}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pangunahing gastos ng PEC ay nagmumula sa variance amplification. Ang variance ng PEC estimator ay lumalaki ayon sa:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Var}\\!\\left(\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right) \\propto \\gamma^2,\n"
"$$\n"
"na nagpapahiwatig ng:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\boxed{\\text{Required number of shots} \\;\\propto\\; \\gamma^2.}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This scaling is fundamental and cannot be improved through classical post-processing.\n"
msgstr "Pundamental ang scaling na ito at hindi mapapabuti sa pamamagitan ng classical post-processing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For circuits containing many noisy gates, each gate contributes a factor $\\gamma_k > 1$, causing the total quasi-probability norm to grow approximately multiplicatively:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma_{\\mathrm{total}} \\sim \\prod_{k=1}^{d} \\gamma_k,\n"
"$$\n"
"where $d$ is the circuit depth. On IBM Quantum hardware, this typically leads to exponential growth in sampling cost with circuit depth, with particularly strong sensitivity to two-qubit gate errors. This scaling places practical limits on the applicability of PEC.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa mga circuit na may maraming noisy na gate, bawat gate ay nag-aambag ng factor na $\\gamma_k > 1$, kaya humigit-kumulang multiplicative ang paglaki ng kabuuang quasi-probability norm:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma_{\\mathrm{total}} \\sim \\prod_{k=1}^{d} \\gamma_k,\n"
"$$\n"
"kung saan ang $d$ ay ang circuit depth. Sa IBM Quantum hardware, karaniwang humahantong ito sa exponential na paglaki ng sampling cost kasabay ng circuit depth, na may partikular na malakas na sensitibidad sa mga two-qubit gate error. Nagtatakda ang scaling na ito ng mga praktikal na limitasyon sa applicability ng PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is currently practical only when one or all of the following conditions are met:\n"
msgstr "Kasalukuyang praktikal lang ang PEC kapag natugunan ang isa o lahat ng sumusunod na kondisyon:\n"

