# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC's relationship to other mitigation methods {#pecs-relationship-to-other-mitigation-methods}"
msgstr "Ugnayan ng PEC sa iba pang mitigation method {#pecs-relationship-to-other-mitigation-methods}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many other mitigation techniques trade accuracy for scalability; PEC does just the opposite, focusing on accuracy above all else.\n"
msgstr "Maraming ibang mitigation technique ang isinasakripisyo ang accuracy kapalit ng scalability; kabaligtaran ang ginagawa ng PEC, na nakatuon sa accuracy higit sa lahat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because PEC might only be used on a subcircuit, it is especially important here to ask what other mitigation methods can be combined with it. To reason clearly about compatibility with PEC, it helps to categorize techniques by what they do to the noise. Consider these general categories:\n"
msgstr "Dahil maaaring gamitin ang PEC sa isang subcircuit lang, lalong mahalagang itanong dito kung anong ibang mitigation method ang puwedeng pagsamahin dito. Para malinaw na maunawaan ang compatibility sa PEC, makakatulong na pangkatin ang mga technique ayon sa ginagawa nila sa noise. Isaalang-alang ang mga pangkalahatang kategoryang ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise cancellation - attempt to invert error channels\n"
msgstr "Noise cancellation - sinusubukang i-invert ang mga error channel\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise scaling - deliberately increase noise to extrapolate\n"
msgstr "Noise scaling - sadyang pinapalaki ang noise para mag-extrapolate\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise reshaping - change the structure or spectrum of noise\n"
msgstr "Noise reshaping - binabago ang estruktura o spectrum ng noise\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bias removal - correct errors that do not scale with gate noise\n"
msgstr "Bias removal - itinatama ang mga error na hindi nag-i-scale sa gate noise\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC sits squarely in category (1). Any method that changes or rescales the noise channel must be examined carefully.\n"
msgstr "Nasa kategorya (1) mismo ang PEC. Ang anumang method na nagbabago o nagre-rescale ng noise channel ay kailangang suriing mabuti.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summary table (high-level)\n"
msgstr "Summary table (high-level)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Technique | Compatible with PEC | Notes |\n"
"|-----------|---------------------|-------|\n"
"|    ZNE    | No | Undoing versus scaling and sometimes tailoring error |\n"
"|   Pauli twirling | Yes (with care) | Affects error behavior, but might make it easier to learn |\n"
"| TREX | Yes | No overlap in workflow. Fully compatible. |\n"
"|Dynamical decoupling | Usually no | Changes error channel |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Technique | Compatible sa PEC | Mga Tala |\n"
"|-----------|---------------------|-------|\n"
"|    ZNE    | Hindi | Pag-undo laban sa pag-scale at minsan pag-tailor ng error |\n"
"|   Pauli twirling | Oo (nang may ingat) | Nakakaapekto sa behavior ng error, pero maaaring mas madali itong matutunan |\n"
"| TREX | Oo | Walang overlap sa workflow. Ganap na compatible. |\n"
"|Dynamical decoupling | Karaniwang hindi | Binabago ang error channel |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and ZNE address the same error sources (gate errors) via mutually incompatible assumptions or workstreams, or both. For example, in ZNE, we assume error can be expanded in a parameter $\\lambda$:\n"
"$$\n"
"E(\\lambda) = E(0) + c_1 \\lambda + c_2 \\lambda^2 + \\cdots\n"
"$$\n"
"and that the error can be effectively scaled to model this expansion. PEC would undo the very error we rely on for the scaling. The parameter $\\lambda$ would become meaningless. Another way of thinking about it is:\n"
msgstr ""
"Tinutugunan ng PEC at ZNE ang parehong pinagmumulan ng error (gate errors) sa pamamagitan ng mga assumption o workstream na hindi magkatugma, o pareho. Halimbawa, sa ZNE, ipinapalagay nating mapapalawak ang error sa isang parameter na $\\lambda$:\n"
"$$\n"
"E(\\lambda) = E(0) + c_1 \\lambda + c_2 \\lambda^2 + \\cdots\n"
"$$\n"
"at mabisang ma-scale ang error para i-model ang expansion na ito. I-u-undo ng PEC ang mismong error na inaasahan natin para sa scaling. Mawawalan ng saysay ang parameter na $\\lambda$. Isa pang paraan ng pag-iisip dito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying ZNE before PEC changes the noise channel you are trying to invert.\n"
msgstr "Ang pag-apply ng ZNE bago ang PEC ay nagbabago sa noise channel na sinusubukan mong i-invert.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying PEC before ZNE removes the very noise ZNE relies on to extrapolate.\n"
msgstr "Ang pag-apply ng PEC bago ang ZNE ay inaalis ang mismong noise na inaasahan ng ZNE para mag-extrapolate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC and ZNE should be considered alternative error-mitigation paradigms, not composable layers. Comparing them side-by-side is instructive, while combining them is not.\n"
msgstr "Dapat ituring ang PEC at ZNE bilang magkahaliling error-mitigation paradigm, hindi mga composable na layer. Kapaki-pakinabang ang pagkumpara sa kanila nang magkatabi, pero hindi ang pagsasama sa kanila.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and Pauli twirling are generally compatible and often beneficial.\n"
"Twirling might help PEC in that twirling converts coherent errors into stochastic Pauli errors. This simplifies the noise channel, making it easier to represent and invert. For PEC, this is extremely valuable, for the following reasons:\n"
msgstr ""
"Karaniwang compatible ang PEC at Pauli twirling at madalas na kapaki-pakinabang.\n"
"Maaaring makatulong ang twirling sa PEC dahil kino-convert ng twirling ang mga coherent error tungo sa stochastic Pauli error. Pinapasimple nito ang noise channel, kaya mas madali itong irepresenta at i-invert. Para sa PEC, napakahalaga nito dahil sa mga sumusunod na dahilan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quasi-probability decompositions are much simpler for Pauli channels\n"
msgstr "Mas simple ang mga quasi-probability decomposition para sa mga Pauli channel\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quasi-probability norm $\\gamma$ is often significantly smaller\n"
msgstr "Ang quasi-probability norm na $\\gamma$ ay madalas na mas maliit nang malaki\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampling variance is reduced\n"
msgstr "Nababawasan ang sampling variance\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Many PEC demonstrations assume or build in Pauli-twirled noise.\n"
"It's important to clarify that Pauli twirling does not mitigate errors by itself; it reshapes noise into a form that probabilistic error cancellation can handle more efficiently.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maraming PEC demonstration ang nag-aassume o nagbi-build-in ng Pauli-twirled na noise.\n"
"Mahalagang linawin na hindi nagmi-mitigate ng error ang Pauli twirling nang mag-isa; binabago nito ang hugis ng noise sa anyong mas mahusay na mahahawakan ng probabilistic error cancellation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC can and should be combined with TREX. These approaches are fully compatible and play orthogonal roles. TREX operates only at measurement, removes readout bias via randomized twirls of the measurement channel, and does not affect gate noise or circuit dynamics. PEC operates on gate noise. Because measurement error is additive rather than compositional, it is independent of gate sequences. It is safe and often desirable to apply TREX alongside PEC.\n"
msgstr "Puwede at dapat pagsamahin ang PEC at TREX. Ganap na compatible ang mga approach na ito at may magkahiwalay na papel. Sa measurement lang gumagana ang TREX, inaalis nito ang readout bias gamit ang randomized twirl ng measurement channel, at hindi nito naaapektuhan ang gate noise o ang circuit dynamics. Sa gate noise gumagana ang PEC. Dahil additive ang measurement error at hindi compositional, hindi ito nakadepende sa mga gate sequence. Ligtas, at madalas na kanais-nais, na i-apply ang TREX kasabay ng PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ordering of these methods is what you might expect:\n"
"1. Execute PEC-randomized circuit\n"
"2. Apply TREX to mitigate readout error\n"
"3. Apply PEC weighting and averaging\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagkakasunod-sunod ng mga method na ito ay ayon sa maaasahan mo:\n"
"1. I-execute ang PEC-randomized na circuit\n"
"2. I-apply ang TREX para i-mitigate ang readout error\n"
"3. I-apply ang PEC weighting at averaging\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and DD are generally incompatible unless the noise characterization used for PEC is performed with DD active. PEC assumes that $N\\text{hardware noise} = \\mathcal N$\n"
"is stationary, repeatable, and accurately characterizable. DD explicitly reshapes the noise channel in time by modulating system-environment interactions and introducing non-trivial pulse-timing effects. As a result, the effective noise with DD is not the same channel as without DD. This is made even more complex by the fact that the noise channel can depend sensitively on circuit scheduling. The end result is that noise inversion becomes ill-defined or invalid.\n"
msgstr ""
"Karaniwang hindi compatible ang PEC at DD maliban kung isinagawa ang noise characterization na ginamit para sa PEC habang aktibo ang DD. Ipinapalagay ng PEC na ang $N\\text{hardware noise} = \\mathcal N$\n"
"ay stationary, paulit-ulit, at tumpak na ma-characterize. Tahasang binabago ng DD ang hugis ng noise channel sa paglipas ng oras sa pamamagitan ng pag-modulate ng mga interaksyon ng system at environment at pagpapakilala ng mga non-trivial na pulse-timing effect. Bilang resulta, hindi pareho ang channel ng effective noise na may DD at wala. Mas pinapakumplikado pa ito ng katotohanang maaaring sensitibong nakadepende ang noise channel sa circuit scheduling. Ang kinalabasan ay nagiging ill-defined o invalid ang noise inversion.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is theoretically possible to characterize noise with DD active and build a PEC model accordingly, but this is highly advanced and not currently a recommended workflow.\n"
msgstr "Teoretikal na posibleng i-characterize ang noise habang aktibo ang DD at bumuo ng PEC model ayon dito, pero lubhang advanced ito at hindi kasalukuyang inirerekomendang workflow.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying PEC by hand {#applying-pec-by-hand}"
msgstr "Manu-manong pag-apply ng PEC {#applying-pec-by-hand}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is complex and it is not recommended that you implement it by hand. Still, we want to work through the math of a basic application on a single qubit to understand what steps the process entails. We choose a mixed but nontrivial state so that we can see numerical effects clearly.\n"
msgstr "Komplikado ang PEC at hindi inirerekomendang i-implement ito nang mano-mano. Gayunpaman, gusto nating daanan ang math ng isang basic na aplikasyon sa iisang qubit para maunawaan kung anong mga hakbang ang kasama sa proseso. Pumili tayo ng mixed pero nontrivial na state para malinaw nating makita ang mga numerical effect.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Take a qubit that should be in the pure state\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi \\rangle & = \\cos(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 1\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{2}\\lvert 1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kumuha ng qubit na dapat ay nasa pure state na\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi \\rangle & = \\cos(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 1\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{2}\\lvert 1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ideal density matrix is:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{ideal}} = \\lvert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\rvert\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ideal na density matrix ay:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{ideal}} = \\lvert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\rvert\n"
"=\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
"We've chosen this density matrix because it is not diagonal and is only for a single qubit so that it is tractable to examine \"by hand\".\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Pinili natin ang density matrix na ito dahil hindi ito diagonal at para sa iisang qubit lang, kaya madaling suriin \"nang mano-mano\".\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now apply a very simple, but realistic noise model: a single-qubit depolarizing channel, with small strength $p$.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = (1 - p)\\rho + \\frac{p}{3}\n"
"(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon ay mag-a-apply tayo ng napakasimple pero makatotohanang noise model: isang single-qubit depolarizing channel, na may maliit na lakas na $p$.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = (1 - p)\\rho + \\frac{p}{3}\n"
"(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To keep the arithmetic friendly, take $p = 0.15$. This channel is completely positive, trace-preserving (CPTP), as it must be. It is a realistic noise channel for real hardware, or at least realistic for describing some of the noise. Further, this noise channel is analytically invertible, as a linear map. In other words, there exists an inverse matrix, but that doesn't mean that the matrix corresponds to a CPTP physical channel, and it certainly doesn't correspond to a unitary that could be implemented on hardware.\n"
msgstr "Para maging madali ang arithmetic, kunin ang $p = 0.15$. Completely positive, trace-preserving (CPTP) ang channel na ito, gaya ng dapat. Isa itong makatotohanang noise channel para sa totoong hardware, o kahit man lang makatotohanan sa paglalarawan ng ilan sa noise. Bukod dito, analytically invertible ang noise channel na ito, bilang linear map. Sa madaling salita, may inverse matrix, pero hindi ibig sabihin nito na tumutugma ang matrix sa isang CPTP physical channel, at tiyak na hindi ito tumutugma sa isang unitary na maaaring i-implement sa hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we apply our depolarizing noise channel to our single-qubit density matrix and obtain:\n"
"$$\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\left(1 - \\frac{4p}{3}\\right)\\rho\n"
"+ \\frac{2p}{3} I.\n"
"$$\n"
"With $p = 0.15$: $\\frac{4p}{3} = 0.20$ and $\\frac{2p}{3} = 0.10$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon ina-apply natin ang ating depolarizing noise channel sa ating single-qubit density matrix at nakukuha ang:\n"
"$$\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\left(1 - \\frac{4p}{3}\\right)\\rho\n"
"+ \\frac{2p}{3} I.\n"
"$$\n"
"Kapag $p = 0.15$: $\\frac{4p}{3} = 0.20$ at $\\frac{2p}{3} = 0.10$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = 0.8 \\rho + 0.1 I.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"So:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = 0.8 \\rho + 0.1 I.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying this to our state:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pag-apply nito sa ating state:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0.8\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"0.1\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"0.8\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"0.1\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute explicitly:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Kalkulahin nang tahasan:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad \\text{(rounded)}.\n"
"$$\n"
"This is still a physical density matrix, and it still has trace one &mdash; but it is more mixed now.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad \\text{(rounded)}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Physical density matrix pa rin ito, at trace one pa rin &mdash; pero mas mixed na ito ngayon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we compute the ideal inverse channel, but being very prepared for the possibility that it might not be physical. We will check whether it is. Mathematically, the inverse linear map is:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\rho - 0.1 I\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon ay kakalkulahin natin ang ideal na inverse channel, pero handang-handa sa posibilidad na maaaring hindi ito physical. Susuriin natin kung physical nga ito. Sa matematika, ang inverse linear map ay:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\rho - 0.1 I\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If this inverse action were itself a valid physical channel, then we would be tempted to try to implement it exactly. Of course, we would still need to figure out how to implement it using unitary operations and classical steps, but implementing this would be the goal. However, it turns out this is *not* CPTP, and there is generally no guarantee that such inverse mappings will be CPTP. That is critical to our current discussion, because it is the reason PEC exists.\n"
msgstr "Kung ang inverse action na ito mismo ay isang valid na physical channel, matutukso tayong subukang i-implement ito nang eksakto. Siyempre, kailangan pa rin nating alamin kung paano ito i-implement gamit ang mga unitary operation at classical step, pero iyon ang magiging layunin. Gayunpaman, lumalabas na *hindi* ito CPTP, at sa pangkalahatan ay walang garantiyang magiging CPTP ang mga ganitong inverse mapping. Kritikal ito sa kasalukuyan nating talakayan, dahil ito ang dahilan kung bakit umiiral ang PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You might be able to see that it is not CPTP just by looking at it. A sure-fire check is to apply it to a density matrix and see if it returns physical results. This is left as an exercise to check your understanding.\n"
msgstr "Maaaring makita mong hindi ito CPTP sa pagtingin lang dito. Ang tiyak na paraan ng pagsuri ay i-apply ito sa isang density matrix at tingnan kung physical ang ibinabalik na resulta. Ito ay iniiwan bilang ehersisyo para suriin ang pag-unawa mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-2}"
msgstr "Suriin ang iyong pag-unawa {#check-your-understanding-2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check whether the inverse mapping from above $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ is CPTP by applying it to a new density matrix:\n"
msgstr "Suriin kung CPTP ang inverse mapping na $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ mula sa itaas sa pamamagitan ng pag-apply nito sa isang bagong density matrix:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{test}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{test}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.95 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.05\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.95 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.05\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Interpret the results as being physical or non-physical.\n"
msgstr "Bigyang-kahulugan ang mga resulta kung physical o non-physical ang mga ito.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_{\\text{test}}) & = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\rho_{\\text{test}} - 0.1 I\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 0.95 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.05 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 0.1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix} 1.0625 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -0.0625 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_{\\text{test}}) & = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\rho_{\\text{test}} - 0.1 I\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 0.95 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.05 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 0.1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix} 1.0625 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -0.0625 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a physical density matrix, this corresponds to a classical probability of greater than 1 that the system is in the state $|0\\rangle$ and a negative probability of being in the state $|1\\rangle$. Clearly this mapping can yield nonsense density matrices. Further, by inspection we can see that the eigenvalues of the resulting density matrix are 1.0625 and -0.0625, meaning not all eigenvalues are positive. Thus the mapping is not \"completely positive\", the \"CP\" in CPTP.\n"
msgstr "Bilang isang physical density matrix, tumutugma ito sa classical probability na higit sa 1 na nasa state na $|0\\rangle$ ang system at negatibong probability na nasa state na $|1\\rangle$. Malinaw na maaaring magbunga ang mapping na ito ng mga walang katuturang density matrix. Bukod dito, sa pagsusuri ay makikita nating ang mga eigenvalue ng nagresultang density matrix ay 1.0625 at -0.0625, ibig sabihin hindi lahat ng eigenvalue ay positibo. Kaya hindi \"completely positive\" ang mapping, ang \"CP\" sa CPTP.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check by explicit calculation that the inverse operation above $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ undoes the noise channel and returns the noise-free state.\n"
msgstr "Suriin sa pamamagitan ng tahasang kalkulasyon na ina-undo ng inverse operation na $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ sa itaas ang noise channel at ibinabalik ang noise-free na state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply it to the noisy state:\n"
msgstr "I-apply ito sa noisy na state:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{recovered}} & = \\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_\\text{noisy})\\\\\n"
" & =\\frac{1}{0.8} \\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"-\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{recovered}} & = \\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_\\text{noisy})\\\\\n"
" & =\\frac{1}{0.8} \\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"-\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.6 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.2\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& \\approx\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.75 & 0.433 \\\\\n"
"0.433 & 0.25\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"This is exactly the original state (up to rounding).\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.6 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.2\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& \\approx\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.75 & 0.433 \\\\\n"
"0.433 & 0.25\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"Eksakto itong ang orihinal na state (hanggang sa rounding).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We restate to be absolutely clear: we cannot invert the noise channel exactly; the inverse is not CPTP, nor is it a valid physical channel. However, we can effectively invert the channel as a linear combination of physical channels.\n"
msgstr "Inuulit natin para maging lubos na malinaw: hindi natin kayang i-invert nang eksakto ang noise channel; hindi CPTP ang inverse, at hindi rin ito valid na physical channel. Gayunpaman, mabisa nating ma-invert ang channel bilang linear combination ng mga physical channel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the depolarizing channel:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I}\n"
"+ \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"where: $\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X$ etc.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa depolarizing channel:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I}\n"
"+ \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"kung saan: $\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X$ at iba pa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The inverse can be written as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}=\\sum_j \\eta_j \\mathcal{P}_j\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang inverse ay maaaring isulat bilang:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}=\\sum_j \\eta_j \\mathcal{P}_j\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with:\n"
msgstr "with:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\mathcal{P}_j$ = physically implementable Clifford channels\n"
msgstr "$\\mathcal{P}_j$ = mga physically implementable na Clifford channel\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\eta_j$ = quasi-probabilities\n"
msgstr "$\\eta_j$ = mga quasi-probability\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some $\\eta_j < 0$\n"
msgstr "Some $\\eta_j < 0$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the core idea behind PEC:\n"
msgstr "Ito ang pangunahing ideya sa likod ng PEC:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample channels according to $|\\eta_j|$∣\n"
msgstr "Mag-sample ng mga channel ayon sa $|\\eta_j|$∣\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Attach signs to measurement outcomes\n"
msgstr "Maglagay ng mga sign sa mga measurement outcome\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expectation values converge to the noise-free value\n"
msgstr "Nagko-converge ang mga expectation value sa noise-free na halaga\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We apply PEC \"by hand\" to the estimation of $\\langle Z \\rangle$ by using the density matrix $\\rho_\\text{noisy}$ and see if we can recover the results for $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$. For $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$ we expect:\n"
msgstr "Ina-apply natin ang PEC \"nang mano-mano\" sa pagtantya ng $\\langle Z \\rangle$ gamit ang density matrix na $\\rho_\\text{noisy}$ at tinitingnan kung mababawi natin ang mga resulta para sa $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$. Para sa $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$, inaasahan natin ang:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} & =\\text{Tr}(Z \\rho_\\text{ideal})\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n"
"&=0.5\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} & =\\text{Tr}(Z \\rho_\\text{ideal})\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n"
"&=0.5\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note also that for the noisy density matrix, we obtain:\n"
msgstr "Pansinin din na para sa noisy na density matrix, nakukuha natin ang:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{noisy} & =\\text{Tr}\\left(Z \\rho_\\text{noisy}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=0.7-0.3\\\\\n"
"&=0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{noisy} & =\\text{Tr}\\left(Z \\rho_\\text{noisy}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=0.7-0.3\\\\\n"
"&=0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It's the right order of magnitude but significantly far from the ideal case.\n"
msgstr "Tama ang order of magnitude pero malayo nang husto sa ideal na kaso.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we step through how, with the PEC process, we can reconstruct the unbiased expectation value from the noisy density matrix. In real workflows, this is probabilistic and will be automated. In this \"by-hand\" workflow, we will choose probabilistic values that are realistic, but perhaps convenient for our presentation. This should not be taken as a claim that PEC is perfect. This is simply to show you a plausible scenario that could happen inside the PEC packages.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon ay daanan natin kung paano, gamit ang proseso ng PEC, mare-reconstruct ang unbiased na expectation value mula sa noisy na density matrix. Sa totoong mga workflow, probabilistic ito at awtomatiko. Sa \"by-hand\" na workflow na ito, pipili tayo ng mga probabilistic na halaga na makatotohanan, pero marahil maginhawa para sa presentasyon natin. Hindi ito dapat ituring na pag-aangkin na perpekto ang PEC. Ipinapakita lang nito ang isang kapani-paniwalang senaryo na maaaring mangyari sa loob ng mga PEC package.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that our noise channel is of the form:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I} + \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"The inverse can be written (exactly):\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na ang ating noise channel ay may anyong:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I} + \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"Ang inverse ay maaaring isulat (nang eksakto) bilang:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"based on symmetry of the transformation and the completeness of the Pauli operators. Inverting the noise channel somehow in the estimation process should yield an estimator that is unbiased and normalized. To do this, we must at least determine the coefficents $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ and then think about how to implement the inverse transformation. When done by a noise learner, the inversion of this noise channel would be done at the channel level, independent of a specific case like our density matrix. The coefficients $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ would come from this inversion.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"based on symmetry of the transformation and the completeness of the Pauli operators. Inverting the noise channel somehow in the estimation process should yield an estimator that is unbiased and normalized. To do this, we must at least determine the coefficents $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ and then think about how to implement the inverse transformation. When done by a noise learner, the inversion of this noise channel would be done at the channel level, independent of a specific case like our density matrix. The coefficients $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ would come from this inversion.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is simpler for this introduction to focus on the channel's effect on our density matrix. This allows us to work with familiar objects like density matrices and expectation values. To that end, consider what must be true about the effects of this inverse operation on our estimation process: the estimator produced by PEC must be normalized and unbiased. This corresponds to two conditions:\n"
msgstr "Mas simple para sa introduksyong ito na tumuon sa epekto ng channel sa ating density matrix. Pinapayagan tayo nitong gumamit ng mga pamilyar na bagay gaya ng density matrix at expectation value. Para dito, isaalang-alang kung ano ang dapat totoo tungkol sa mga epekto ng inverse operation na ito sa ating estimation process: ang estimator na nagagawa ng PEC ay dapat normalized at unbiased. Tumutugma ito sa dalawang kondisyon:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normalization: To ensure that this operation does not change the scale of the observable, we require that $\\alpha+3\\beta = 1$. To see why this is the case, we could either consider the action of the inverse on a density matrix, or consider its action on the expectation value of something trivial like $\\mathcal{I}$ itself.\n"
msgstr "Normalization: Para matiyak na hindi nagbabago ang scale ng observable sa operation na ito, kailangan nating $\\alpha+3\\beta = 1$. Para makita kung bakit ganito, maaari nating isaalang-alang ang aksyon ng inverse sa isang density matrix, o ang aksyon nito sa expectation value ng isang trivial na bagay gaya ng $\\mathcal{I}$ mismo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calibration: In a real workflow, we use calibration circuits to learn noise behavior at a gate level. We then use the gate-level knowledge of noise behavior, and the linearity of expectation values to apply the learned noise model to the larger circuit. In our case, we started with artificial knowledge that the ideal expectation value $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0.5$. But it would be very easy to come up with a state for which we know theoretically that this would be the ideal value, and then use actual measurements for calibration. A key point is that for PEC, one typically does not learn a full noise model of the entire circuit. Instead, one learns local noise models for individual gates or circuit layers and uses those to construct the quasi-probability decomposition.\n"
msgstr "Calibration: Sa totoong workflow, gumagamit tayo ng mga calibration circuit para matutunan ang noise behavior sa antas ng gate. Ginagamit natin pagkatapos ang kaalaman sa noise behavior sa antas ng gate, at ang linearity ng mga expectation value, para i-apply ang natutunang noise model sa mas malaking circuit. Sa ating kaso, nagsimula tayo sa artipisyal na kaalaman na ang ideal na expectation value ay $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0.5$. Pero napakadaling mag-isip ng state na alam nating teoretikal na ito ang ideal na halaga, at saka gumamit ng aktwal na mga measurement para sa calibration. Isang mahalagang punto na para sa PEC, karaniwang hindi natututunan ang buong noise model ng buong circuit. Sa halip, natututunan ang mga local noise model para sa mga indibidwal na gate o circuit layer at ginagamit ang mga iyon para buuin ang quasi-probability decomposition.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use these conditions to determine $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. We consider the ansatz\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit natin ang mga kondisyong ito para tukuyin ang $\\alpha$ at $\\beta$. Isaalang-alang ang ansatz na\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"and apply it to an arbitrary single-qubit density matrix $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"and apply it to an arbitrary single-qubit density matrix $\\rho$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that the Pauli channels act by conjugation:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Y}(\\rho) = Y\\rho Y, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Z}(\\rho) = Z\\rho Z.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na ang mga Pauli channel ay kumikilos sa pamamagitan ng conjugation:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Y}(\\rho) = Y\\rho Y, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Z}(\\rho) = Z\\rho Z.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ to $\\rho$ gives:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pag-apply ng $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ sa $\\rho$ ay nagbibigay ng:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\rho\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\left(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\rho\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\left(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Taking the trace, we obtain:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"&=\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\Big(\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(X\\rho X)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Y\\rho Y)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Z\\rho Z)\n"
"\\Big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pagkuha ng trace, nakukuha natin ang:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"&=\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\Big(\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(X\\rho X)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Y\\rho Y)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Z\\rho Z)\n"
"\\Big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each Pauli operator is unitary, such that conjugation preserves the trace:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(P\\rho P) = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho),\n"
"\\qquad P \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Unitary ang bawat Pauli operator, kaya pinapanatili ng conjugation ang trace:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(P\\rho P) = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho),\n"
"\\qquad P \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Therefore,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(\\alpha + 3\\beta)\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"(\\alpha + 3\\beta)\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the PEC estimator to be normalized, the effective\n"
"inverse map must preserve the trace of all density matrices. That is, we require:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Para maging normalized ang PEC estimator, dapat panatilihin ng effective\n"
"inverse map ang trace ng lahat ng density matrix. Ibig sabihin, kailangan natin ng:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"\\qquad \\text{for all } \\rho.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"\\qquad \\text{for all } \\rho.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies the normalization constraint:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\alpha + 3\\beta = 1.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinahihiwatig nito ang normalization constraint:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\alpha + 3\\beta = 1.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "But in our case, this yields the condition:\n"
msgstr "Pero sa ating kaso, nagbubunga ito ng kondisyong:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"& =\n"
"\\alpha(+0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(+0.4)\n"
"& = 0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"& =\n"
"\\alpha(+0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(+0.4)\n"
"& = 0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we use calibration information to relate the observed expectation value to the known ideal one.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon ay gumagamit tayo ng calibration information para iugnay ang naobserbahang expectation value sa kilalang ideal na halaga.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{ideal}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{ideal}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0.5\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"0.5\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Or equivalently,\n"
"$$\n"
"0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)=0.5\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Or equivalently,\n"
"$$\n"
"0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)=0.5\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solving our two conditions for $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, we obtain:\n"
msgstr "Sa paglutas ng ating dalawang kondisyon para sa $\\alpha$ at $\\beta$, nakukuha natin ang:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"\\beta = -0.0625\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"\\beta = -0.0625\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These coefficients sum to 1, but one of them is negative.\n"
msgstr "Ang kabuuan ng mga coefficient na ito ay 1, pero isa sa mga ito ay negatibo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can recover the ideal expectation value by randomly modifying the circuit, measuring, multiplying the result by a signed weight, and averaging. In particular, no density matrices are reconstructed and no inverse channel is implemented physically.\n"
msgstr "Mababawi natin ang ideal na expectation value sa pamamagitan ng random na pagbabago sa circuit, pag-measure, pagpaparami ng resulta sa isang signed na weight, at pag-average. Sa partikular, walang density matrix na nire-reconstruct at walang inverse channel na pisikal na ini-implement.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The key step: this is PEC {#the-key-step-this-is-pec}"
msgstr "Ang pangunahing hakbang: ito ang PEC {#the-key-step-this-is-pec}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For our noise strength $p=0.15$, the inverse channel can be written as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1} =\\underbrace{1.1875}_{\\alpha}\\,\\mathcal{I}\n"
"\\;+\\;\n"
"\\underbrace{(-0.0625)}_{\\beta}\n"
"(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa ating noise strength na $p=0.15$, ang inverse channel ay maaaring isulat bilang:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1} =\\underbrace{1.1875}_{\\alpha}\\,\\mathcal{I}\n"
"\\;+\\;\n"
"\\underbrace{(-0.0625)}_{\\beta}\n"
"(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Important facts:\n"
msgstr "Mahahalagang katotohanan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The coefficients sum to 1\n"
msgstr "Ang kabuuan ng mga coefficient ay 1\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "One coefficient is negative\n"
msgstr "Isang coefficient ang negatibo\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each term is physically implementable\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat term ay physically implementable\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The negativity moves into classical post-processing\n"
msgstr "Ang negativity ay lumilipat sa classical post-processing\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We form a sampling distribution from the absolute values of the weights:\n"
msgstr "Bumubuo tayo ng sampling distribution mula sa mga absolute value ng mga weight:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\alpha| = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"|\\beta| = 0.0625\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\alpha| = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"|\\beta| = 0.0625\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(for each of X, Y, Z)\n"
msgstr "(para sa bawat isa sa X, Y, Z)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Total weight:\n"
"$$\n"
"W = 1.1875 + 3\\times0.0625 = 1.375\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kabuuang weight:\n"
"$$\n"
"W = 1.1875 + 3\\times0.0625 = 1.375\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For sampling probabilities, divide by W.\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga sampling probability, hatiin sa W.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Operation | Probability | Sign |\n"
"|-----------|-------------|------|\n"
"| Do nothing ($\\mathcal{I}$) |1.1875 / 1.375 ≈ 0.864 |+ |\n"
"| Apply X | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Apply Y | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Apply Z | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Operation | Probability | Sign |\n"
"|-----------|-------------|------|\n"
"| Walang gagawin ($\\mathcal{I}$) |1.1875 / 1.375 ≈ 0.864 |+ |\n"
"| I-apply ang X | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| I-apply ang Y | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| I-apply ang Z | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The sign comes from the original coefficient, not the probability.\n"
msgstr "Ang sign ay galing sa orihinal na coefficient, hindi sa probability.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each shot consists of these steps:\n"
msgstr "Binubuo ang bawat shot ng mga sumusunod na hakbang:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the state\n"
msgstr "Ihanda ang state\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let the hardware apply the noisy circuit\n"
msgstr "Hayaang i-apply ng hardware ang noisy na circuit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Randomly choose an operation from the table above using the associated probabilities\n"
msgstr "Random na pumili ng operation mula sa table sa itaas gamit ang kaugnay na mga probability\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply it\n"
msgstr "Apply it\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure $Z$, getting $\\pm 1$\n"
msgstr "I-measure ang $Z$, na nagbibigay ng $\\pm 1$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiply the outcome by $\\text{sign} \\times W$\n"
msgstr "I-multiply ang outcome sa $\\text{sign} \\times W$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Record that number\n"
